    dict(key='12-act-5', kind='console', title='Act Five — The same algorithm for every type',
         body='FIVE. The same algorithm for every type.\n  <Integer> reverse(): 12 pointer changes; head -> 1200 <-> 930 <-> 610 <-> 540 <-> 820 <- tail\n  <String>  reverse(): 12 pointer changes, the very same code\n  already in Java: java.util.LinkedList<E>, a generic doubly linked list with head and tail',
         narration='One algorithm for every type. [[slnc 400]] Reverse swaps the pointers of every node, then head and tail. [[slnc 400]] Twelve pointer changes for the sizes, and the same twelve for the names. [[slnc 500]] Generics change the type, not the algorithm.'),
